The mounting bracket is a 6" x 24" x 0.5" plate,
represented by the 4.684" equivalent OD pipe, 12"
on each side of boom. These elements are capable of
withstanding 93 mph winds without ice; 69 mph winds
with 1/4-inch ice. 

The front-to-rear ratio is better than 13 dB across
the band (better than 20 dB from 7.0 to 7.2 MHz),
and the SWR is better than 3.5:1 across the band 
(better than 1.5:1 from 7.0 to 7.2 MHz), with 
mid-band free-space gain of 7.4 dBi.
